Build uses `CFLAGS = -g -O2 -I/usr/include/libnl3` (no -Werror in the final build — configure was run without those, or the CFLAGS environment variable was overridden at configure time… in any case, the Makefile shows -g -O2). Good — the build is forgiving.

OK, let me set up the TODO list and implement. Plan:

1. **nbdclt.h**: Add `bool persist_mode;`, `int dead_conn_timeout;` to CLIENT. Add typedefs for `saved_connection_t` and `persist_connection_t` (per the gold patch).
2. **nbd-client.c**:
