```

Hmm wait, if reconfigure fails, the connection is dead but the kernel is still disconnected; no further LINK_DEAD events will come (or maybe one more will). The process keeps monitoring. Not much else we can do — acceptable. (Alternatively we could retry the entire cycle. But reconfigure failure indicates a kernel-side issue like device teardown. Leave it and log it. err_code already logs. Actually gold's netlink_reconfigure calls err_code() and EXITs on failure! err_code is noreturn. Hmm — gold's netlink_reconfigure:

```c
	ret = nl_send_sync(socket, msg);
	if (ret < 0) {
		err_code("Failed to reconfigure device, check dmesg\n", ret);
